---
import Eyebrow from '../Eyebrow.astro';
import SectionHeadline from '../SectionHeadline.astro';
---

<section id="compliance" class="py-20 md:py-24" aria-label="The Compliance Moat">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="bg-bg-secondary border border-border rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-12 max-w-4xl">
      <Eyebrow text="04 &middot; THE MOAT" />
      <SectionHeadline>
        The only platform<br>that <em>enforces</em> NCAA rules.
      </SectionHeadline>

      <div class="max-w-[780px] space-y-4">
        <p class="text-text-muted text-base leading-relaxed">
          ScoutStreak doesn't just display recruiting calendars &mdash; it enforces them.
          When a recruiter tries to message an athlete during a dead period, the platform
          blocks the message and logs the attempt. When a contact window opens, coaches
          get notified automatically. Every interaction is timestamped and exportable for
          compliance audits.
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-muted text-base leading-relaxed">
          The compliance calendar is self-managing: sport-specific dead periods, quiet periods,
          contact periods, and evaluation periods are preconfigured for all 14 sports.
          Athletic Directors can export a full audit trail at any time. No other recruiting
          platform offers this.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 bg-poor/[0.06] border border-poor/20 rounded-xl p-6">
        <p class="text-text text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-poor font-600">$2.8B House v. NCAA settlement</span> + NIL regulation
          = Athletic Directors are actively buying compliance tools.
          ScoutStreak is the only platform that <em class="not-italic font-600 text-text">prevents</em>
          violations instead of documenting them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
